<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2a7964f7211f7a2d64d8c56f3f00491350717bc4> <http://schema.org/description> "DONG Energy awarded Offshore Marine Management (OMM) a contract to perform an\r\ninspection survey of the offshore export connecting the Burbo Offshore Wind Farm located\r\nto the shore in Liverpool Bay. This included the BB13 to BB14 inter array power cable.\r\nBurbo Offshore Windfarm is located approximately 8 Kilometres offshore and the shore\r\nlanding is located approximately 1 Kilometre northwest of Wallasey, near Liverpool. The\r\ntotal length of the export and inert array power cables is approximately 26 Kilometres. The report in this series describes the survey operations conducted upon the export and inter array\r\npower cables. The objectives of the operations were:\r\n&gt; Mobilisation of work vessel with all the required navigation, positioning and survey\r\nequipment.\r\n&gt; Cable Survey/Inspection – Entire 3 x Export Cable lengths, A2, B2 and C1 to shore (approx.\r\n8.5 Km each).\r\nInspection Survey of the export cables with shallow water survey system\r\n'ROC.si' (Crawler) operated off the support vessel (Multicat), MCS Ailsa\r\n&gt; Cable Survey/Inspection – BB13 to BB14 Inter-Array Cable (approx. 560m)\r\n&gt; Inspection Survey of the inter array cable with shallow water survey system\r\n'ROC.si' (Crawler) operated off the support vessel (Multicat), MCS Ailsa. A 24-hour working day was adopted for all survey operations." .
_:bae3e007687352dde0185ba6c706d9c2 <http://schema.org/value> "BB14" .
_:b6a9d03ad07e6bf4a6ac483b9b6b4bac <http://schema.org/value> "modiolus" .
